From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Storage Maintainers <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: share allocation admission with strict WAL recovery

Read-only recovery limits must not reject WAL batches that the same policy
previously accepted. Logical live-catalog quotas also cannot bound physical
journal history: preallocation, overwritten records and delayed maintenance
can exceed those quotas without increasing the live catalog.

Add an optional allocation policy checked by every WAL writer before any
batch bytes are written and by normal and strict recovery before decoding.
Reject unsupported Clear operations before WAL changes, preserve the policy
across rotation, and distinguish pre-write allocation refusal from uncertain
I/O failure. Bound journal inventory at creation by postponing rotation at
the configured cap while continuing ordinary flush work. Historical journal
bytes remain streamed rather than charged as simultaneously resident data.
On recovery, skip each keyspace's persisted prefix after decoding and checksum
validation, retaining only unflushed suffixes instead of replaying old history
into memtables. Unset-policy recovery keeps its existing behavior.

Leaving the policy unset preserves existing writer and recovery behavior. Existing
state above a newly selected policy is incompatible and strict inspection
refuses it without repair; the policy does not claim a total database heap
bound or make arbitrary historical data compatible.

---
